      "id": 1,
      "text": "Champaign was founded in 1855 when the Illinois Central Railroad laid tracks two miles west of downtown Urbana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://champaignil.gov/about/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city was originally called West Urbana and received its charter in 1860, becoming Champaign.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champaign%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1999, the Illinois Terminal intermodal center opened, named after a defunct electric interurban line that once ran through town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champaign%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Virginia Theatre, a 1,463‑seat movie palace, opened on December 28, 1921, and has been restored to its former glory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champaign%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The State Farm Center, once the Assembly Hall, now hosts Illinois Fighting Illini basketball teams and is a landmark of campus life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
